<title>MALAYSIA: Bank Negara's reserves rose to 70.60 bln rgt.</title>
<headline>Bank Negara's reserves rose to 70.60 bln rgt.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Negara's gold, foreign exchange and other reserves rose to 70.60 billion ringgit as at January 31, compared with 70.35 billion a fortnight earlier, the Bank said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The central bank said its total assets and liabilities rose to 94.63 billion ringgit from 93.91 billion two weeks earlier.  </p>
<p>(In bln ringgit) Jan 31 1997    Jan 15 1997	Jan 31 1996</p>
<p>Reserves	    70.60	     70.35		61.35</p>
<p>Assets		94.63	     93.91		87.09</p>
<p>Currency	    25.01	     22.40		19.67</p>
<p>Govt paper	   1.88		1.70		 2.17</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 230 8911)</p>
</text>
